\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	h)	}nImO uses two configuration files - nimo-config.txt and nimo-services.txt, stored in '/etc/nimo' or 'C:/nImO' for windows. They are in the form of a text representation of a nImO 'map'; nimo-config.txt can be overridden with any of the command-line tools using the '-c' or '\'97config' command-line option.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The file 'nimo-config.txt' has the following keys and they are all optional:\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li2160\fi-2160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}logger address - the local multicast address to be used for the logger service.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}logger port - the IP port to be used for the logger service, which must be a non-privileged port.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}registry options - the options to be passed to the registry service on startup.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}registry path - the path to the registry service; the string '$$' represents the install location for the nImO executables.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}registry search timeout - the time in seconds to wait before determining that the registry service is unavailable.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}status address - the local multicast address to be used for status messages.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}status port - the IP port to be used for status messages, which must be different from the logger port.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The file 'nimo-services.txt' has keys corresponding to the services that are installed, with values of a map from 'path' to the location of the executable for the service and 'description', a text string that can be displayed.\
